{
  "_comment": "Shapes for tests/unit/test_static_power_filter.py. t_spf_battlecrier is Temur Battlecrier's only printed line, the witness for `power` in a static COUNT filter. t_spf_lord is the same key in an `affects` position -- an anthem that reads power while the anthem layer is running -- which is where a naive `chars()` read would recurse for ever. t_spf_discounter is the card-level `cost_reduction` reader, which runs outside the characteristics pipeline and therefore reads the DERIVED number; it is kept live so the divergence between the two readers is measured rather than asserted in a comment. t_spf_anthem is the thing a static filter must not see, t_spf_runt the 3/3 it pumps to 4 power, t_spf_brute a printed 4/4 and t_spf_bear a printed 2/2. t_spf_tough is the toughness twin.",
